    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "Maintain at least one IPv4 outbound connection through the Tor network",
    "body": "Currently, for sybil resistance, we try to maintain at least one outbound connection to a node from each of the reachable networks.\n\nIf both IPv4 and Tor happen to be reachable, then we can do better at a relatively low cost (considering code volume and complexity) - in addition to the direct IPv4 we try to maintain now, try to have one to IPv4 through the Tor network.\n\nThis would have different properties compared to the direct IPv4 connection - the node's ISP can hijack all direct IPv4 connections and redirect them to their own nodes. The ISP, however, cannot do that for IPv4-via-Tor connections. For that a malicious Tor exit node (or their ISP) is needed, which is usually somewhere else on the internet compared to the node's ISP.\n\nIPv4-via-Tor connections would be complementary to direct-IPv4 connections, not mutually exclusive.\n\nFor IPv6, either:\n* do the same, e.g. maintain at least one connection to IPv4 peer and one to IPv6 peer through the Tor network; or\n* treat IPv4 and IPv6 the same for this - maintain at least one connection to IPv4 or IPv6 peer through the Tor network.",
