      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "I can take a bounded implementation and test contribution; please assign me if this direction is useful. An efficient approach is to treat Tor-proxied IPv4 as a separate outbound-selection goal while preserving the existing direct IPv4/IPv6 diversity, then test selection and reconnect behavior across Tor availability and proxy failure. The less-obvious factor is that Tor reachability is not interchangeable with direct IPv4 reachability: fallback must not silently violate the proxy boundary, and the new goal should not cause connection churn or reduce existing network diversity.",
